    "result_text": "All tests pass. The implementation is complete. Here's a summary of the change:\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required composing a `salutation` from an optional `title` (MR/MRS/MS/DR) plus the owner's `lastName`, returning `title + ' ' + lastName`, or just `lastName` when no title is given.\n\nI made each change where it belongs in this standard Spring Boot layering:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** (contract \u2192 generated DTOs):\n   - Added `title` as an optional input field on `OwnerFields` (the editable request schema).\n   - Added `salutation` as a read-only derived field on `Owner` (the response schema).\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** (domain model):\n   - Added the persisted `title` field with `@Column(name = \"title\")` and its getter/setter.\n   - Added a `@Transient getSalutation()` derived getter, placed alongside the existing name-formatting getters (`getDisplayName`, `getInitials`) \u2014 a small, single-responsibility method that returns `title + \" \" + lastName`, or just `lastName` when the title is null/blank.\n\n3. **DB schemas** (`h2`, `hsqldb`, `postgres`, `mysql`): added the `title` column to the `owners` table so the field persists.\n\nNo mapper or controller changes were needed: MapStruct auto-maps `title` (request \u2192 entity) and `salutation` (entity \u2192 response) by name, and the derived getter reuses the same pattern already established for the other computed owner fields (`getDisplayName`, `getContactPreference`, etc.) rather than duplicating logic.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreComposesSalutation` (creates an owner with `title=DR`, `lastName=who`, expects `salutation == \"DR who\"`) and the full suite are green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
